      "input": {
        "name": "GameCube Controller",
        "_comment": "Four controller ports, each the pad a GameCube ships with. Wire order per pad: A B X Y Z Start Up Down Left Right L R, then Main Stick X/Y, C-Stick X/Y and the two analog trigger travels. The digital L/R bits are the full-press clicks at the bottom of the trigger travel; pressing them reports full analog travel too, the way the real trigger cannot click without being down. After the pads, the console's own controls: Previous Disc and Next Disc move a selector over the project's discs and touch nothing; Disc Swap is the lid - up for as long as it is held, and closing on the selected disc (or, with the selector untouched, on the next one). The selector is there when the project has more than one disc, the lid when it has a disc at all.",
