      "input": {
        "name": "Wii Controllers",
        "_comment": "Four ports. Each holds what its setting says: a GameCube controller, a Wii Remote, a Wii Remote with a Nunchuk, or a Wii Remote with a Classic Controller; the same columns serve all of them, and a name means the same on each. Wire order per port: the GameCube controller's A B X Y Z Start Up Down Left Right L R, then 1 2 Plus Minus Home Shake C ZL ZR; axes Main Stick X/Y, C-Stick X/Y, the two analog trigger travels, then Pointer X/Y and Tilt X/Y. A Wii Remote uses A, B, the d-pad, 1, 2, Plus, Minus, Home, Shake, the pointer and the tilt; a Nunchuk adds C, Z and its stick as the main stick; a Classic Controller has a, b, x, y as A, B, X, Y, the d-pad, L, R, ZL, ZR, Plus, Minus and Home, its left stick as the main stick, its right as the C-stick and its analog L and R as the triggers. Pointer X and Y are where the Wii Remote points, -32768 to 32767 across the screen and down it; Tilt X is right positive and Tilt Y forward positive. After the ports, the console's own controls: Previous Disc and Next Disc move a selector over the project's discs and touch nothing; Disc Swap is the lid - up for as long as it is held, and closing on the selected disc (or, with the selector untouched, on the next one).",
